- id: dhcr_administrative_appeal
  name: DHCR Administrative Appeal
  description: An appeal to the DHCR's Deputy Commissioner or Commissioner from a
    determination by a Rent Administrator in a rent overcharge or other rent regulation
    proceeding.
  jurisdiction: NYS
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id005
  - Administrative Appeal
  - Administrative Appeal to DHCR
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4807583/matter-of-kostic-v-new-york-state-div-of-hous-community-renewal/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/10131664/matter-of-aidekman-v-state-of-ny-div-of-hous-community-renewal/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4832002/matter-of-kostic-v-new-york-state-div-of-hous-community-renewal/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/2759844/corsini-v-morgan/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4680212/matter-of-bedeau-realty-corp-v-state-of-new-york-div-of-hous/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/5997156/73-warren-street-llc-v-state-of-new-york-division-of-housing-community/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/5997157/73-warren-street-llc-v-state-of-new-york-division-of-housing-community/
    sample_quotes:
    - The landlord appealed the DHCR determination to the Commissioner.
    - The landlord appealed the rent administrator's determination to the Deputy Commissioner.
    - The matter was appealed to the Deputy Commissioner, who affirmed the rent administrator's
      finding of no overcharge.
    suggested_aliases: *id005
- id: dhcr_administrative_determination
  name: DHCR Administrative Determination
  description: A procedure to file a letter with DHCR requesting an official determination
    that an apartment is rent stabilized.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id006 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.justfix.org/en/learn/rent-history-101
    sample_quotes:
    - write a letter to DHCR asking for an 'administrative determination' that your
      apartment is rent stabilized
    suggested_aliases: *id006
- id: dhcr_complaint_cooling
  name: DHCR Complaint for Cooling System Failure
  description: An administrative complaint filed with the Division of Homes and Community
    Renewal (DHCR) to address a landlord's failure to maintain a cooling system, potentially
    leading to rent reduction or freeze.
  jurisdiction: NYS
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id007 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.justfix.org/en/learn/air-conditioning-laws
    sample_quotes:
    - you can file a complaint with the State agency that oversees rent stabilization,
      the Division of Homes and Community Renewal (“DHCR”). DHCR may freeze or reduce
      your rent until the landlord corrects the problems.
    suggested_aliases: *id007
- id: dhcr_par_proceeding
  name: DHCR Petition for Administrative Review (PAR)
  description: An administrative appeal to DHCR challenging a rent administrator's
    determination on a rent overcharge or service complaint.
  jurisdiction: NYS
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id008 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/10364727/matter-of-5511-777-st-marks-ave-bk-llc-v-state-of-new-york-div-of-hous/
    sample_quotes:
    - petitioner commenced this CPLR article 78 proceeding to challenge a determination
      of the respondent State of New York Division of Housing and Community Renewal
      (DHCR) which denied its petition for administrative review
    suggested_aliases: *id008
- id: dhcr_rent_decrease_filing
  name: DHCR Rent Decrease Filing
  description: An administrative proceeding to request a rent reduction due to landlord's
    failure to provide services or repairs.
  jurisdiction: NYS
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id009 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/rent-control/
    sample_quotes:
    - the tenant can file for a decrease with the DHCR
    suggested_aliases: *id009
- id: dhcr_rent_history_request
  name: DHCR Rent History Request
  description: An administrative procedure to obtain the rent history of an apartment
    from the New York State Division of Housing and Community Renewal, often by texting
    a specific number.
  jurisdiction: NYS
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id010 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.justfix.org/en/learn/rent-history-101
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/about-rent-stabilization/
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/how-can-i-find-out-if-i-am-rent-stabilized/
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/rent-stabilization-overcharges/
    sample_quotes:
    - JustFix’s Rent History Tool helps you request your rent history from the New
      York State Division of Homes and Community Renewal ('DHCR') via snail mail
    - You can obtain a printout of the registered rents for your apartment – called
      a ‘rent history’ – from the NYS Division of Housing & Community Renewal.
    - Get a copy of your apartment’s rent history from the DHCR by texting “MCH” to
      (855) 610-2450 and following the prompts.
    suggested_aliases: *id010
