- id: supreme_court_declaratory_judgment
  name: Supreme Court Declaratory Judgment Action
  description: A civil action in New York State Supreme Court seeking a judicial declaration
    of the parties' rights, often used in complex landlord-tenant disputes involving
    regulatory status.
  jurisdiction: NYS
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id025
  - Declaratory Judgment Action
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/2170691/mbia-insurance-corp-v-federal-deposit-insurance/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/10360824/independent-435-cpw-tenants-assn-v-park-front-apts-llc/
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/10598390/matter-of-901-bklyn-realty-llc-v-manigat/
    sample_quotes:
    - The tenants brought a declaratory judgment action in Supreme Court, seeking
      a determination that their apartments were subject to rent stabilization.
    - MBIA Insurance Corp. v. Federal Deposit Insurance Corp., 2011 WL 4527400 (D.D.C.
      2011)
    - petitioner commenced this proceeding seeking, among other things, a declaration
      that the rent for the subject apartment was not overcharged
    suggested_aliases: *id025
